wehrdienst-bmg-objection-lichtentanne.tr:
General information
You can apply in writing to exercise the right to object to publication or transfer of personal data.
An objection is possible at any time and remains effective until withdrawn. The transfer block expires when you move away.
The registration authority does not provide written confirmation that the transfer block has been recorded.
You may object to the transfer of your personal data:
• to parties, voter groups and other bodies proposing candidates in connection with parliamentary and municipal representative bodies or use of the data for election advertising;
• to the press, broadcasters and elected representatives for publication of age and wedding anniversaries;
• to address-book publishers and others for publication in address books or similar reference works;
• to public-law religious communities if you do not belong to them;
• to the Bundeswehr Federal Office of Personnel Management for sending information material.
Only with consent may the registration authority transfer data for:
• advertising;
• address trading.

