bafoeg-th-citizenship-condition.tr:
What conditions apply to BAföG?

To be eligible for BAföG, you must:

• be at most 45 years old;
• have German citizenship;

or

be an EU citizen and have a permanent right of residence in Germany, be employed in Germany or be self-employed (there are further special cases for EU citizens).

It must also be a first course of training, for example:
• first university studies after the Abitur;
• studies after an Abitur acquired through second-chance education;
• studies after an apprenticeship completed after the Abitur.

The studies must:
• be full-time;
• be at a state-recognised higher education institution (university, university of applied sciences, academy — including private institutions if state-recognised).

A Master’s course is eligible if it builds on a Bachelor’s course.

