ctx.tr:
Loans
In a particular emergency, the Jobcenter can provide loans as benefits in kind or cash.
Such an emergency can, for example, be:
• a broken washing machine or refrigerator;
• electricity debts or high annual electricity bills, if instalments to the electricity supplier cannot prevent disconnection;
• financial hardship through loss or theft of a wallet.
The loan must then be repaid. As a rule, from the month after approval, 5 percent of the standard need is withheld to repay the loan (offset). In your decision, repayment is shown under payment recipients.
In an urgent financial emergency, arrange an appointment online or by phone with your benefits team (see the three-digit team number at the top right of your decision).
Loans can also be granted in the following cases:
• loans for a rental deposit;
• loans to cover rent arrears;
• loans against expected income.

