Where are passengers’ rights and obligations set out?
Your rights and obligations are set out:
• in the Uniform Rules concerning the Contract for International Carriage of Passengers by Rail (CIV);
• in EC Regulation 1371/2007 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 October 2007;
• in the Conditions of Carriage of ÖBB Personenverkehr AG;
• in the Federal Law Gazette of the Republic of Austria, Part I, BGBl 40/2013.
Rules on travel opportunities for people with reduced mobility
Railway undertakings and station operators establish rules so that everyone can use their services. Passengers with reduced mobility should not suffer disadvantages. They should have the same travel opportunities as everyone else. This is set out in passenger rights, Article 19(1).

