ARTICLE7 EXCLUSION OF WITHDRAWAL
1. Where the consumer has no withdrawal right, the trader may exclude it only if clearly stated in the offer or in time before the contract.
2. Exclusion is possible only for products:
a. made to the consumer’s specifications;
b. clearly personal in nature;
c. which by their nature cannot be sent back;
d. which can quickly perish or become obsolete;
e. whose price depends on financial-market fluctuations outside the trader’s control;
f. individual newspapers and magazines;
g. audio/video recordings and computer software whose seal the consumer broke.
3. Exclusion is possible only for services:
a. accommodation, transport, restaurant or leisure activities on a set date or period;
b. whose performance began with express consumer consent before the cooling-off period expired;
concerning betting and lotteries.

