Foreign residents can acquire German nationality through naturalisation.
As a rule, the following requirements must be met:
eight years of lawful residence in Germany;
possession of a residence permit or settlement permit, meaning permanent residence;
sufficient German-language knowledge, demonstrated either through the B1 language test and naturalisation test or instead by attending a German general school with at least a sufficient German grade, completing a degree at a German university, or completing vocational training with a vocational-school leaving certificate;
no substantial previous convictions;
sufficient income for oneself and dependent relatives, without relying on benefits under Book II or Book XII of the Social Code;
willingness to give up the previous nationality;
commitment to the free democratic basic order.
Spouses and children can be naturalised together under certain conditions. Special naturalisation requirements apply to some groups.

