The amount of maintenance advance is derived from minimum maintenance.
Minimum maintenance is based on the child’s subsistence minimum and is regularly set by statutory ordinance. Because costs rise as the child grows older, the legislature has determined that minimum maintenance is set at:
87% of the subsistence minimum for children until they reach age six;
100% for children over six until they reach age twelve;
and 117% for older children.
Child benefit for first children, currently 250 euros, which is also paid from public funds, is deducted from those amounts. This produces the following maintenance-advance amounts (as from 1 January 2024):
230 euros for children under six;
301 euros for children aged six and under twelve;
395 euros for children aged twelve and under eighteen.

