The Measles Protection Act has applied since 1 March 2020. It is intended to promote protection against measles in nurseries, schools, other communal institutions and medical facilities.
Certain groups must therefore prove that all measles vaccinations (2) have been administered. These groups are:
• all children from their first birthday before entering nursery or school;
• all people born after 1970 who work in or receive care in a communal institution;
• all people born after 1970 who work in medical facilities;
• asylum seekers and refugees no later than four weeks after admission to communal accommodation.

